# Read by EAS Build when it assembles the project archive to upload.
#
# EAS CLI detects this is a monorepo (apps/native sits under a shared
# pnpm-workspace root) and archives from THIS directory, not from apps/native.
# It does not reliably walk into and apply a workspace package's own nested
# .gitignore the way `git` itself does — so apps/web/.gitignore excluding
# `/.next/` does not stop that directory from being swept into an iOS or
# Android build upload. It's a real cache that regrows every time `pnpm
# dev:web` runs, and it has been the entire reason "eas build --platform ios"
# uploads a ~140MB archive: apps/web/.next alone was 187MB uncompressed,
# 93.5% of everything on disk in this repo, and none of it is native app code.
#
# Mirrors the root .gitignore, restated here because EAS reads this file
# specifically rather than resolving gitignore precedence itself.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
dist
**/dist
build
**/build
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage
.cache
tmp
temp

# apps/native's own build/cache directories. Already covered by
# apps/native/.gitignore, restated here for the same reason as above.
apps/native/android
apps/native/ios
apps/native/.expo
apps/native/web-build

# Design/planning docs — not needed by any build, no reason to upload them.
/plans
/systems
/flows
